            <ArticleTitle>Acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis induced by ingestion of bamifylline.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>634-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis (AGEP) in a 64-year-old woman, associated with the use of bamifylline. To the best of our knowledge there have been no previous reports of AGEP induced by the ingestion of bamifylline in the medical literature. We, therefore, add this drug to the list of causes for AGEP.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
